// Tests hex.ptr_index n (an unsigned hex[:n] index), n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8, 16: indexes 0, 1, the maximum and a
//   random one, on bases near 0, random, and near the top of the address range (the add carries across many
//   hexes, and wraps). Then hex.ptr_index w/4 against hex.ptr_index on random full-width ("negative") indexes.
// Then dst == index at every n. dst starts as garbage, and a garbage hex follows index[:n].
// Expected values are python's (seed 20261024, w=64); each check prints '=' when the result is right.
stl.startup

GARBAGE = 0x5a3c96e15a3c96e15a3c96e15a3c96e1

test_ptr_index_n 1, 0x0, 0x0, 0x0
